RUNTIME PROBES — executed via `php artisan tinker --execute` against the scratch
database `wacademy_audit_scratch` (created for this audit; the dev DB `wacademy`
was never touched). No application file was created, modified or deleted.

================================================================================
PROBE A — student photo route signature (AUDIT.md finding P0-1)
================================================================================
Command:
  DB_DATABASE=wacademy_audit_scratch php artisan tinker --execute='
    $s = App\Models\Student::first();
    echo route("students.photo",$s);
    echo Illuminate\Support\Facades\URL::signedRoute("students.photo",["student"=>$s->id]);
    $req = Illuminate\Http\Request::create(route("students.photo",$s),"GET");
    var_export($req->hasValidSignature());
  '

Output:
  student: id=1 photo_path=NULL
  route()       : http://localhost/students/1/photo
  signedRoute() : http://localhost/students/1/photo?signature=a91bd892e7a53f0e957c131fdba96d226ecfc0e1036e7fd027fe7d87c5bbd0bf
  middleware    : web,auth,signed
  hasValidSignature on route() URL: false
  hasValidSignature on signed URL : true

Interpretation: the route is registered with the `signed` middleware
(Illuminate\Routing\Middleware\ValidateSignature). Every caller in
resources/views builds the URL with route(), which produces an UNSIGNED URL for
which hasValidSignature() is false. ValidateSignature aborts 403.

================================================================================
PROBE B — API token creation (AUDIT.md finding P0-2)
================================================================================
Command:
  DB_DATABASE=wacademy_audit_scratch php artisan tinker --execute='
    $u = App\Models\User::first();
    var_export(method_exists($u,"createToken"));
    var_export(Schema::hasTable("personal_access_tokens"));
    $u->createToken("probe");
  '

Output:
  User traits: HasAttributes, HasEvents, HasGlobalScopes, HasRelationships,
    HasTimestamps, HasUniqueIds, HidesAttributes, GuardsAttributes,
    PreventsCircularRecursion, ForwardsCalls, HasCollection, Authenticatable,
    Authorizable, CanResetPassword, MustVerifyEmail, HasFactory, HasRoles,
    LogsActivity, Notifiable, SoftDeletes, HasPermissions,
    HasDatabaseNotifications, RoutesNotifications
  has createToken method: false
  personal_access_tokens table exists: false
  createToken FAILED -> BadMethodCallException: Call to undefined method App\Models\User::createToken()

Interpretation: App\Models\User does NOT use Laravel\Sanctum\HasApiTokens, and no
migration creates personal_access_tokens (confirmed against the migrated scratch
schema — see 17-schema.log and the table listing below). POST /api/v1/auth/login
therefore throws before returning a token.

Tables present after `migrate:fresh --seed` (no personal_access_tokens):
  activity_log, agreement_signatures, agreement_templates, attendances, cache,
  cache_locks, coaches, failed_jobs, framework_pillars, framework_strike_levels,
  guardian_student, guardians, job_batches, jobs, migrations,
  model_has_permissions, model_has_roles, permissions, role_has_permissions,
  roles, sessions, squad_student, squads, students, training_sessions, users

================================================================================
PROBE C — agreement signature immutability (AUDIT.md finding P1-4)
================================================================================
Command: created a probe AgreementSignature row in the scratch DB, attempted to
rewrite the fields the spec treats as write-once, then force-deleted the row.

Output:
  after mass-assign update(): TAMPERED
  IMMUTABLE via update()? false
  signed_at re-writable? true
  status re-writable?    true
  probe row removed.

Interpretation: `template_snapshot`, `signed_at` and `status` are all listed in
AgreementSignature::$fillable (app/Models/AgreementSignature.php:19-34) with no
`saving`/`updating` guard, no `$guarded` protection and no DB-level trigger.
A signed agreement record can be silently rewritten after the fact.

================================================================================
PROBE D — route middleware stacks (AUDIT.md findings P1-3, P1-6)
================================================================================
Command: php artisan route:list --json | (decode, print uri/name/middleware)

Relevant rows:
  agreement/{student}           agreement.show      web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:guardian
  agreement/{student}           agreement.sign      web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:guardian
  agreement/{student}/download  agreement.download  web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:guardian
  portal                        guardian.dashboard  web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:guardian,EnsurePasswordChanged,EnsureAgreementSigned
  student                       student.dashboard   web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:student,EnsurePasswordChanged,EnsureAgreementSigned
  coach                         coach.dashboard     web,Authenticate,RoleMiddleware:coach,EnsurePasswordChanged
  students/{student}/photo      students.photo      web,Authenticate,ValidateSignature
  api/v1/children               api.v1.children     api,Authenticate:sanctum
  api/v1/schedule               api.v1.schedule     api,Authenticate:sanctum
  dashboard                     dashboard.redirect  web,Authenticate

Interpretation:
  - EnsureAgreementSigned IS applied to both the guardian and student groups.
  - The agreement routes themselves carry NO EnsurePasswordChanged, so a
    guardian still on the admin-issued first-login password can sign.
  - The API routes carry NO EnsureAgreementSigned and NO EnsurePasswordChanged.
  - students.photo carries ValidateSignature but no EnsurePasswordChanged.

================================================================================
PROBE E — query counts (AUDIT.md finding P2-15, N+1)
================================================================================
Seed volume in the scratch DB: students=4, squads=2, sessions=2, attendances=4
(DemoDataSeeder). The guardian under test has 1 linked child, so these numbers
are a floor, not a stress measurement.

  GuardianDashboard (1 child)                   : 6 queries
  EnsureAgreementSigned accessor loop (1 child) : 3 queries
  Coach squad roster (2 students)               : 1 query
  Coach squads w/ active_student_count accessor : 3 queries

Interpretation: the per-child work in GuardianDashboardController::index
(app/Http/Controllers/Guardian/GuardianDashboardController.php:16-40) issues one
next-session query and one attendance query per child inside a ->map() closure,
and Student::getHasSignedCurrentAgreementAttribute
(app/Models/Student.php:92-104) issues an AgreementTemplate::current()->first()
plus an exists() per call. Both scale linearly with the number of children.
The absolute counts above are small only because the demo seed is small.

================================================================================
PROBE F — filesystem disk configuration (AUDIT.md IS-9.3)
================================================================================
  public disk root : storage/app/public
  default disk     : local
  storage/app/      contains: private/  public/
  public/storage symlink: NOT present
  Storage::url / asset('storage' / '/storage/' references in app+views: 0 hits

Interpretation: student photos and drawn signatures are written to the `local`
disk, whose Laravel 11 default root is storage/app/private. Nothing is exposed
through a public URL. The private-storage requirement holds; only the delivery
route is broken (Probe A).
